'' AN '#if' LEFT OPEN AT THE END OF A FILE IS AN ERROR IN A COMPILE, not only under
'' --pp-only. fbc refuses it (error 290, 'Expected #ENDIF', measured 2026-09-27); a compile
'' accepted it, because the parser stops at the EOF and the preprocessor's end-of-input check
'' never ran. The check now runs when the root file's EOF is reached (src/pp/ppmodule.bas).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --emit-ir tests/diagnostics/src/open-if-compile.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: open-if-compile.bas(2,1): error TKO0303: '#if' has no matching '#endif'
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 1
